From fcadc4c00dec19f23fc4423d308a5018c1a15606 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Adrien Delmas <adrien@adriendelmas.com>
Date: Sun, 25 Oct 2026 04:46:59 +0100
Subject: [PATCH 144/144] hydra: Karma Physical Sky, and
 karma:global:enable_dof

The Karma Physical Sky LOP reaches Hydra as a generic `light` whose kma
shader is KMAskyDomeLight (the dome), or as a `karmaSkyAtmosphere` prim
carrying Karma's scattering coefficients as primvars (the atmosphere),
plus a distant light for the sun. Neither was a type the delegate created:
the sky was black. Both render as a dome on Cycles' sky texture now.

The dome uses Hosek-Wilkie, Karma's own model: 1.00 of Karma on every
patch at sun altitudes 10, 30 and 60 degrees (tools/bench_sky.py). The
atmosphere uses the multiple-scattering sky lit by the scene's distant
light (the session tracks the sun as its light syncs, every atmosphere
rebuilds on it), Karma's Rayleigh, Mie and ozone coefficients converted to
densities, and a measured scale of 0.0041: 0.88-1.25 of Karma per patch.
Not carried over: aerial perspective, observer altitude, other scale
heights (a warning). An unknown Karma light renders nothing instead of a
white point light. (K-104)

Depth of field: Karma blurs whenever the f-stop is above zero unless the
render settings write disableDepthOfField (already read) or
karma:global:enable_dof = false, which husk forwards to every renderer;
the second counts now. (K-105)

Co-Authored-By: Claude Fable 5.1 <noreply@anthropic.com>
